# Studio Demo Automation - Configuration

Load studio-specific configurations from JSON or environment variables.

Example studios.config.json:

```json
{
  "studios": [
    {
      "id": "studio-1",
      "name": "Production Studio",
      "url": "https://app.example.com/studios/1",
      "expectedTitle": "Studio 1",
      "authRequired": true,
      "authCredentials": {
        "email": "${STUDIO_EMAIL}",
        "password": "${STUDIO_PASSWORD}"
      },
      "features": [
        {
          "name": "Open Dashboard",
          "description": "Load the dashboard",
          "action": { "type": "waitForSelector", "selector": ".dashboard" },
          "validate": [
            { "type": "visible", "selector": ".dashboard", "description": "Dashboard loaded" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Description | Default |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `STUDIO_URLS` | Comma-separated URLs to override config | None |
| `TEST_STUDIO_ID` | Run only a specific studio by ID | All studios |
| `VIDEO_CONVERT` | Convert WebM to MP4 post-run | false |
| `STUDIO_EMAIL` | Email for studio authentication | - |
| `STUDIO_PASSWORD` | Password for studio authentication | - |
| `BASE_URL` | Base URL for the application | http://localhost:3000 |
